INSERT INTO feature VALUES('completion','rewriting','Knuth–Bendix and Squier completion','cell-rewriting','implemented','unique','dependent provers','A rule system is completed under a budget, its derived cells carrying replayable coherence certificates, declining with a report where it cannot; a critical pair whose sides part fills the diagnostics model''s obstruction shape, and its refusal names the peak and both normal forms. Each step of a certificate records the substitution that matched its cell, on the peak skolemized; the replay instantiates the cell by it in place of a match, and refuses a forged substitution by name. On a presented reading, completion skips the join of each composite pair, whose peak holds a redex strictly below its seam, and keeps that redex as the pair''s witness, which the replay checks. The critical triples of a store are listed once each: three steps on one peak that the overlaps of their left-hand sides connect. On each unary corpus block, they are the essential cells of dimension four of Brown''s collapse. The homotopy basis of a convergent store with linear cells reduces by its critical triples as a Morse collapse: the boundary of each triple''s 4-cell is built from the confluences and the outermost normal forms within a budget, a confluence that occurs there once, at the root and with no context, is removed through the rest of the boundary, and the reduct carries its equivalence, whose replay runs each witness; on B₃⁺ it keeps A and B and removes C and D, as Example 7.5.8 of the polygraphs book states, a boundary past the budget pairs nothing, and a cell that copies or erases a variable is refused.','theory-coherent-resolutions theory-computads surface-diagnostics','crates/theory-coherent-resolutions/tests/completion.rs crates/theory-coherent-resolutions/tests/triple.rs crates/theory-coherent-resolutions/tests/basis.rs crates/surface-lowering/tests/squier.rs',NULL,NULL);
